1
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:16,000
Adventure begins with a Z.

2
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:26,000
The Legend of Zorro is a action, adventure, western
film directed by Martin Campbell.

3
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Despite trying to keep his swashbuckling to a minimum, a threat to California's pending statehood
causes the adventure-loving Don Alejandro de la Vega and his wife, Elena, to take action.

4
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Don Alejandro de la Vega / Zorro, played by Antonio Banderas.

5
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:56,000
Elena, played by Catherine Zeta-Jones.

6
00:43:00,000 --> 00:43:06,000
Joaquin, played by Adrian Alonso.

7
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:16,000
Frey Felipe, played by Julio Oscar Mechoso.

8
00:57:20,000 --> 00:57:26,000
Jacob McGivens, played by Nick Chinlund.

9
01:04:30,000 --> 01:04:36,000
Lupe, played by Alexa Benedetti.

10
01:11:40,000 --> 01:11:46,000
The Legend of Zorro is a 2005 American Western swashbuckler film
directed by Martin Campbell, produced by Walter F.

11
01:18:50,000 --> 01:18:56,000
Parkes, Laurie MacDonald and Lloyd Phillips, with music by James
Horner, and written by Roberto Orci and Alex Kurtzman.

12
01:26:00,000 --> 01:26:06,000
It is the sequel to 1998's The Mask of Zorro; Antonio Banderas and Catherine Zeta-Jones reprise their roles as
the titular hero and his spouse, Elena, and Rufus Sewell stars as the villain, Count Armand.

13
01:33:10,000 --> 01:33:16,000
The film takes place in San Mateo County, California and was shot in San Luis
Potosí, Mexico, with second-unit photography in Wellington, New Zealand.

14
01:40:20,000 --> 01:40:26,000
The film was theatrically released on October 28, 2005, by Columbia Pictures (instead of TriStar
due to Columbia holding the sequel rights to TriStar's pre-1999 film library).

15
01:47:30,000 --> 01:47:36,000
The Legend of Zorro earned $142.4 million on a $75 million budget.

16
01:54:40,000 --> 01:54:46,000
It received poor reviews, with critics generally praising its acting, but
criticizing the screenplay, special effects, tone and humor.

17
02:01:50,000 --> 02:01:56,000
The film explores themes of california, hero, mexico,
parent child relationship, marriage crisis.
